  "id": "DrugBank_DB04572 - MONDO_6335",
  "verbalization": "Thiotepa, a chemotherapy agent, is linked to Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma through a chain of indications that involve other cancers and drugs. The evidence suggests that Thiotepa may be used in the treatment of Ovarian Carcinosarcoma, which in turn is associated with Melphalan and Tretamine, both of which are linked to Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma. This implies a potential indirect relationship where Thiotepa could influence the progression or treatment of this cancer through the intermediaries of these other entities. The shared pathway involves the use of chemotherapy agents in the management of ovarian malignancies, suggesting a possible role in the treatment of Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, highlighting a possible mechanism involving chemotherapy in the context of ovarian cancer treatment.",
